  <content>
  <section><para>Complete the following questions to practice the skills you have learned in this lesson. Double click on mathematical
  expressions/equations to enlarge. If needed, use the “^” symbol to enter an exponent.</para>
<!--Do not edit this div tag.  It must surround the interaction block-->
<section class="check-understanding"><exercise data-content-id="54828607-798d-48f4-9098-8816f83d3f26"><problem><para>
      <para>Whenever the input of a function \(f\) increases by 1, the output increases by 5. Which of these equations
          could define \(f\)?</para>
      </para><para>Multiple Choice:</para><para>\(f(x)=3x+5\)</para><para>\(f(x)=5x+3\)</para><para>\( f(x)=5^x\)</para><para>\( f(x)=x^5\) </para></problem><solution><para>\(f(x)=5x+3\)</para><para>
      <para>The correct answer is \(f(x)=5x+3\).
      </para>
    </para></solution></exercise></section></section>
</content>
</document>
